WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.119
Look at this map of the Moon.

00:00:02.119 --> 00:00:07.966
Every yellow marker is a place humans have been, or robots from Earth have been.

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:10.596
Twelve of those markers were people.

00:00:10.596 --> 00:00:11.912
Tranquillity Base.

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:13.081
Ocean of Storms.

00:00:13.081 --> 00:00:13.812
Fra Mauro.

00:00:13.812 --> 00:00:14.762
Hadley Rille.

00:00:14.762 --> 00:00:16.223
Descartes Highlands.

00:00:16.223 --> 00:00:17.320
Taurus-Littrow.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.851
Six Apollo landing sites, between July 1969 and December 1972.

00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:26.235
Three and a half years from first footstep to last footstep.

00:00:26.235 --> 00:00:29.378
Gene Cernan was the commander of Apollo 17.

00:00:29.378 --> 00:00:36.539
He was the eleventh person to walk on the Moon, and the second-to-last back into the lunar module.

00:00:36.539 --> 00:00:59.121
The very last person was Cernan himself — he was the commander, so he climbed up the ladder behind his crewmate, took one last look at the surface, and then he said this: "As we leave the Moon at Taurus-Littrow, we leave as we came, and, God willing, as we shall return — with peace, and hope for all mankind.

00:00:59.121 --> 00:01:02.117
" "Godspeed the crew of Apollo Seventeen.

00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:04.382
" That was December 14th, 1972.

00:01:04.382 --> 00:01:13.444
Gene Cernan died in 2017, having lived almost his entire adult life as the most recent person to set foot on another world .

00:01:13.444 --> 00:01:19.144
As of the moment you are listening to this, more than fifty years have passed.

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:23.894
In that half century, three Mars rovers have been built and sent.

00:01:23.894 --> 00:01:27.622
Two space stations have been continuously occupied.

00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:30.033
One probe has gone interstellar .

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:32.737
And nobody has been back to the Moon.

00:01:32.737 --> 00:01:35.149
Artemis II is in flight planning.

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:42.018
If it flies on schedule, Cernan's title — last person on the Moon — will pass to someone else.

00:01:42.018 --> 00:01:48.961
Until that happens, every time you look at this map, twelve markers represent a closed chapter.

00:01:48.961 --> 00:01:52.176
A chapter we are still trying to open again.

